(Problem Context: A concrete cube of weight W = 500 N rests on a rough ramp inclined at) Tj
T*
(theta = 30 deg to the horizontal. Coefficient of static friction is mu_s = 0.35.) Tj
T*
(Determine the range of horizontal force P applied to the block such that it remains in) Tj
T*
(static equilibrium \(neither slides down nor slips up\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Case A - Impending motion DOWN the incline \(minimum force P_min\):) Tj
T*
(Friction acts UP the incline: F = mu_s * N.) Tj
T*
(Normal Reaction: N = W*cos\(30\) + P*sin\(30\) = 500*0.8660 + P*0.5 = 433.01 + 0.5*P.) Tj
T*
(Equilibrium along incline: P*cos\(30\) + mu_s * N - W*sin\(30\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(P*0.8660 + 0.35 * \(433.01 + 0.5*P\) - 500*0.50 = 0.) Tj
T*
(0.8660*P + 151.55 + 0.1750*P - 250 = 0 => 1.0410*P = 98.45 => P_min = 94.57 N.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Case B - Impending motion UP the incline \(maximum force P_max\):) Tj
T*
(Friction acts DOWN the incline: F = mu_s * N.) Tj
T*
(Normal Reaction: N = 433.01 + 0.5*P.) Tj
T*
(Equilibrium along incline: P*cos\(30\) - mu_s * N - W*sin\(30\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(P*0.8660 - 0.35 * \(433.01 + 0.5*P\) - 250 = 0.) Tj
T*
(0.8660*P - 151.55 - 0.1750*P - 250 = 0 => 0.6910*P = 401.55 => P_max = 581.11 N.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: For static equilibrium, the horizontal force P must satisfy: 94.57 N <= P <=) Tj
T*
(581.11 N.) Tj
