T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A uniform ladder of length L = 6.0 m and weight W_L = 300 N rests) Tj
T*
(against a smooth vertical wall at an inclination angle of theta = 60 deg with the rough) Tj
T*
(horizontal ground \(mu_floor = 0.30\). A structural inspector of weight W_p = 750 N climbs) Tj
T*
(up the ladder. Calculate how far up along the ladder \(distance x from the base\) the) Tj
T*
(inspector can safely climb before the ladder begins to slip.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Support reactions at base A and wall B:) Tj
T*
(At smooth wall B: Normal reaction N_B is perpendicular to wall \(horizontal\); friction) Tj
T*
(F_B = 0.) Tj
T*
(At rough floor A: Vertical reaction N_A; horizontal friction F_A directed toward the) Tj
T*
(wall.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Global Equilibrium equations:) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fy = 0 => N_A - W_L - W_p = 0 => N_A = 300 + 750 = 1050 N.) Tj
T*
(At impending slipping at base A: F_A = F_lim = mu_floor * N_A = 0.30 * 1050 = 315 N.) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fx = 0 => N_B - F_A = 0 => N_B = 315 N.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Moment Equilibrium about base point A \(Sigma M_A = 0\):) Tj
T*
(Clockwise moments from weights = Counterclockwise moment from wall reaction N_B:) Tj
T*
([ W_L * \(L/2\) * cos\(60\) ] + [ W_p * x * cos\(60\) ] - [ N_B * L * sin\(60\) ] = 0.) Tj
T*
([ 300 * 3.0 * 0.50 ] + [ 750 * x * 0.50 ] - [ 315 * 6.0 * 0.8660 ] = 0.) Tj
T*
(450 + 375 * x - 1636.74 = 0 => 375 * x = 1186.74 => x = 3.16 m.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: The inspector can safely climb up to distance x = 3.16 m along the ladder) Tj
T*
(before slip occurs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
