(phi = atan\(mu\) = atan\(0.25\) = 14.04 deg.) Tj
T*
(Wedge angle alpha = 15.0 deg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Equilibrium of the vertical block \(pier\):) Tj
T*
(Forces on block: Weight W = 25 kN downward; vertical guide reaction R1 inclined at phi =) Tj
T*
(14.04 deg to normal; interface reaction R2 from wedge inclined at phi = 14.04 deg to) Tj
T*
(normal of wedge face \(total angle from vertical = alpha + phi = 15 + 14.04 = 29.04 deg\).) Tj
T*
(Using Lami's or force polygon on block: R2 * cos\(alpha + phi + phi\) or vertical) Tj
T*
(equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fx = 0 => R1*cos\(phi\) - R2*sin\(alpha + phi\) = 0 => R1 = R2 * sin\(29.04\) /) Tj
